{
  "dom_id": "step-q336186",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The position $s(t)$ of a particle (in inches) at time $t$ minutes is given by \n\n$$\ns(t)=3{t}^{4}-4{e}^{t},\\,t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nCalculate the speed of the particle when $t=0\\,\\text{min}.$\n\nThe speed of the particle is \n{{field-1}}$\\text{in/min}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{4}-4{e}^{t}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{3}-4{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $t=0,$ the velocity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(0) & =12\\cdot {0}^{3}-4{e}^{0} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed is $|-4|=4\\,\\text{in/min}.$",
